sections.instructions:
Define up to 3 SMART objectives and expected results. Each result must be explicitly linked to at least one GIFR KPI indicator using the codes listed below: 

KPI 1 – Resilience and Dignified Life Outcomes:
1a Shelter Solutions – number of individuals or families receiving adequate shelter;
1b Health Service Coverage – percentage of beneficiaries with access to essential health services;
1c WASH Access – number of beneficiaries with access to safe water and sanitation;
1d Cash Assistance – volume of assistance and number of beneficiaries.

KPI 2 – Economic Empowerment and Sustainable Development:
2a Livelihood Outcomes – number of individuals securing employment or starting businesses;
2b Educational Outcomes – number of beneficiaries enrolled or completing education/training.

KPI 3 – Programmatic Adaptability and Environmental Sustainability:
3a Emergency Response Agility – time to approve funding;
3b Climate Action Integration – number/percentage of projects integrating climate or green solutions.

KPI 4 – Geographic and Demographic Inclusivity:
4a Target Group Reach – proportion of refugees, IDPs, stateless people, and host communities;
4b Exceptional Programs – projects outside IsDB geography.

KPI 5 – Program Accountability and Reporting:
5a Implementation Progress – rate of execution and funds disbursed;
5b Fund Misuse/Refund – amount refunded;
5c Donor Engagement – reporting frequency and transparency.

Develop a full logical framework using ONLY the KPI list below as reference. Each row must include a valid KPI code (e.g., 1a, 2b, 3b).

KPI LIST:
1a Shelter Solutions;
1b Health Service Coverage;
1c WASH Access;
1d Cash Assistance;
2a Livelihood Outcomes;
2b Educational Outcomes;
3a Emergency Response Agility;
3b Climate Action Integration;
4a Target Group Reach;
4b Exceptional Programs;
5a Implementation Progress;
5b Fund Misuse/Refund;
5c Donor Engagement.
